   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Organization for Migration (IOM)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting Protection of Migrant Workers Globally Through Advisory Services To Private and Public Actors</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Under the Migration, Business, and Human Rights in Asia Programme (MBHR Asia), IOM actively strives to promote the protection of the human and labour rights of migrant workers through fair and ethical recruitment, as well as to eliminate forced labour, human trafficking, and other rights violations faced by migrant workers. With significant technical expertise on issues related to MBHR, IOM aims to increase its international engagement with partners, particularly business enterprises operating in all sectors and of all sizes. The goal is to support these enterprises in adhering to their obligations under Pillars 2 and 3 of the United Nations Guiding Principles on Business and Human Rights (UNGP), ensuring the respect of migrant workers&apos; rights and providing remediation when harm occurred.</narrative>
  </description>
